19
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:26,300
It's written as a journey. A journey is a story the business side recognizes, which, um, doubles as a test the builder can execute.

20
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:27,340
Oh, got it.

21
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:31,160
And it has three mandatory parts. Number one, where it starts.

22
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:33,000
Okay. Number two, the steps.

23
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:35,840
And number three, what counts as finished.

24
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:36,340
Right.

25
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,220
So in the fictional country of these examples, Progressa,

26
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:44,400
what are the exact steps the change of name journey is written to take?

27
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:50,560
So we look at the five specific steps of Progressa's journey for approving a change of an institution's name.

28
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:57,320
Number one, a test officer at the ministry, MoEYS Mm-hmm... signs in with the minister's role.

29
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:05,000
Number two, she opens the names list, um, and chooses the advice for Harbourview University College.

30
00:02:05,260 --> 00:02:06,200
Okay. Step two.

31
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:10,699
Number three, she reads the advice from the quality authority, PHEQA.

32
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:13,960
PHEQA, right. Number four, she approves the new name.

33
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:20,860
And number five, the journey is finished only when the approval is recorded, um, and sent back to PHEQA.

34
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:24,760
So when your minister requires concrete evidence of acceptance,

35
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:27,140
what must the record of the run name?

36
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:30,040
Well, the record of the run must name four things.

37
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:35,020
Uh, number one, which journey. Okay. Number two, on which installation.

38
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:36,860
Number three, at what time.

39
00:02:37,540 --> 00:02:40,320
And, um, number four, with what result at each step.

40
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,440
What if, um, what if a journey is written but not run,

41
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:46,160
like they ran out of time?

42
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:50,940
A journey written but not run is reported strictly as not run.

43
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:56,760
Ministers sign records of what actually happened, uh, not descriptions of what should happen.

44
00:02:57,400 --> 00:03:02,020
Okay. So what will the recording show when the demonstration of this journey takes place?

45
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:07,420
The recording will show the test officer signing into the live installation with the minister's role.

46
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:17,360
Right. It will show her executing each step of the change of name journey, and the test will pass only when the system generates the factual record of the run- Mm-hmm... confirming the

47
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:20,780
approval is successfully recorded and sent back to PHEQA.

48
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:23,460
So just to be absolutely clear,

49
00:03:24,540 --> 00:03:28,200
what constitutes true acceptance of a system under this method?

50
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:36,080
True acceptance of a system only ends when a person finishes a real task on the running service and generates a record of the run.
